.\" Manpage for ia_repack.
.TH IA_REPACK 1 "2026-10-28" "ia_repack 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ia_repack \- replace named archive.org folders with uncompressed tar files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ia_repack.py
.I IDENTIFIER FOLDER
.RI [ FOLDER ...]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Processes explicit folder paths sequentially in their given order. Each folder
is an exact item-relative filename prefix. The workflow downloads and verifies
all selected files, creates an uncompressed tar, reads back every member to
verify its size and MD5, uploads the tar into the same item, and confirms its
size and MD5 in IA metadata before deleting any remote source files.
.PP
parent/folder becomes parent/folder.tar. Members retain full item-relative
paths. Originals are deleted only with --delete-originals. Deletion is limited
to the frozen source list, with cascade deletion disabled. The tar and source
snapshot are rechecked before each delete. New or changed sources stop the
workflow. A different existing remote tar is never overwritten.
.PP
Keep the work directory after interruption or failure and re-run the same
command. The journal allows partially completed deletions to resume without
downloading again. Failure stops processing before the next folder.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Plan only. Write nothing locally or remotely; credentials are unnecessary.
.TP
.B --delete-originals
Delete remote source files after confirming the uploaded tar. Without this,
remote sources are retained.
.TP
.B --yes, -y
Confirm remote source deletion for unattended operation.
.TP
.B --clean-local
Remove generated downloads and local tar after successful remote operations,
before moving to the next folder. Journals remain. Without this option, local
files are retained.
.TP
.BI --workdir " PATH"
Persistent workspace (default .ia_repack_IDENTIFIER). Allow about twice the
current folder's size during packing, plus any retained earlier folders.
.TP
.BI --log " PATH"
Append redacted logs outside the workspace. Ignored in dry runs.
.TP
.BI --retries " N"
Attempts per request or verification poll (default 12).
.TP
.BI --retry-wait " SEC"
Initial exponential backoff (default 15).
.TP
.BI --max-retry-wait " SEC"
Backoff ceiling before jitter (default 600).
.TP
.BI --wait-between " SEC"
Pause between folders (default 0).
.TP
.BI --connect-timeout " SEC"
Connection timeout (default 30).
.TP
.BI --read-timeout " SEC"
Download/metadata/delete read inactivity timeout (default 60). Tar uploads
use ia_upload's size-based response timeout.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
IA write credentials configured with ia configure, and published size and MD5
for every source file. Avoid editing selected folders while a run is active.
Metadata can lag accepted uploads or deletions; retain the workspace and
re-run later if confirmation retries run out.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete; 1 transfer, verification or local I/O failure; 2 invalid usage or
unsafe/changed source paths; 130 interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ia_repack.py my-item 'folder one' 'parent/folder two' --dry-run
ia_repack.py my-item 'folder one' 'parent/folder two' \\
    --delete-originals --yes --clean-local --log repack.log
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ia_download (1), ia_upload (1)
